  <descriptions>
    <description xml:lang="en" descriptionType="Abstract">Race results of every FIA Formula One World Championship Grand Prix from 1950-05-13 to 2025-12-07 (76 seasons, 1149 Grands Prix, 25,873 driver entries, 817 drivers, 203 constructor entries, 77 circuits in 34 countries). The dataset is a cleaned, documented derivative of the Ergast database as served by the Jolpica-F1 API. Duplicates, missing keys, sentinel values, inconsistent identifiers and free-text categories were resolved; legitimate historical shared drives were kept and flagged; ISO 3166 country codes and Wikidata identifiers were added.</description>
    <description xml:lang="en" descriptionType="Methods">Extracted from racing_f1_data.zip (Zenodo DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23416916; SHA-256 81b027c4221901d92d30ad7b76eacf22668d299098e5c16dcb391c91fd39c748) without modifying values, profiled across completeness, uniqueness, validity, consistency, accuracy and timeliness, and cleaned with a reproducible Python/pandas pipeline that logs before/after statistics for every step. Source code, audit log and quality report are part of the package.</description>
    <description xml:lang="en" descriptionType="TechnicalInfo">UTF-8 encoded CSV (RFC 4180), comma separated, header row, ISO 8601 dates. Primary key of the fact table: result_id. Column definitions in data_dictionary.csv and datapackage.json.</description>
    <description xml:lang="en" descriptionType="Other">Points follow the scoring rules of each season; use points_normalised for cross-era comparisons. Indianapolis 500 rounds (1950-1960) are flagged with is_indy500. The raw archive this package is derived from has the DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23416916; the curated package is prepared for deposit in Zenodo as its own record, and the DOI shown for it is a placeholder until minted.</description>
  </descriptions>
